Z||000006||fierosound||07-02-2001||08:27 PM||||Thanks for the comments everybody.  I plan to post BETTER pictures on my website later.<P>sjp777...  I replaced my rear quarter windows and had tinit film applied before installing them on the car.  Tint film can be applied on installed windows.  Just be sure to remove the black trim piece surrounding them first.<P>MRGONE... absolutely correct<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 07-02-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000007||88CoupeV6||07-02-2001||08:42 PM||||Wow, It looks super sweet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I know you will love the tires. I have the same type. Good product.<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000008||sjp777||07-02-2001||09:13 PM||||I asked about getting the sail panel windows tinted when I did the door glass. The guy wouldn't do it because those windows are exposed to the elements on both sides. He said eventually the moisture would cause the tint to seperate.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tonker||07-02-2001||09:42 PM||||Looks really nice...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Re: the sail panel windows, mine seem to be cracking and starring a bit. Is this common? Is it easy to replace them? Cost?<P>Thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierosound||07-05-2001||12:01 AM||||sjp777...<BR>I was told the same thing, and had it done anyway.  They wouldn't warranty the quarter windows.  The tint stayed on and looked pretty good for about 7 years.  It can be removed and redone at that time.  I just replaced the windows when I repainted the car (one was cracked anyway).<P>Tonker...<BR>GM still makes windows for the GT.  Any GM dealer can give you a price (expensive).  I went with repro windows from Fiero Warehouse <A HREF="http://geocities.com/fierowarehouse/gtwindows.html" TARGET=_blank>http://geocities.com/fierowarehouse/gtwindows.html</A>  .  Installation is easy, getting the old windows off is hard.  F/W also has already tinted quater windows available.<p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||10
